%% State Pattern Class Diagram
%% Allows object to alter behavior when internal state changes

classDiagram
    class Context {
        -state State
        +Context(State)
        +setState(State) void
        +request() void
    }
    
    class State {
        <<interface>>
        +handle(Context) void
    }
    
    class ConcreteStateA {
        +handle(Context) void
    }
    
    class ConcreteStateB {
        +handle(Context) void
    }
    
    class ConcreteStateC {
        +handle(Context) void
    }
    
    class Client {
        +main() void
    }
    
    Context --> State : has current
    State <|.. ConcreteStateA
    State <|.. ConcreteStateB
    State <|.. ConcreteStateC
    ConcreteStateA ..> Context : may transition
    ConcreteStateB ..> Context : may transition
    ConcreteStateC ..> Context : may transition
    
    note for Context "Delegates state-specific\nbehavior to current State.\nState objects can trigger\ntransitions."
